Test wiring: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/Widgets/SentryEventLogWidgetTests.cs (65 tests); the Model/
  ViewModel/Source are <Compile Include .. Link> into the headless net10.0 test project (the established
  pattern used by AlertFeed/AuditLog/etc.) so the WinUI-free logic is verified without a UI host.

Parity covered (web -> native):
  * deriveEvent precedence: door open -> sentry on -> sentry off -> locked -> unlocked -> state updated.
  * subtitle (wide only): lock + sentry state joined ' · ' or '—'; web hex accents mapped to design tokens.
  * eventLimit = isWide?10:isTall?7:4 applied as the projection cap (WidgetEventFeed maxItems); vehicle_id
    scopes the request (sibling convention: ChargeHistory WindowLimit / AlertFeed MaxItems).
  * all 6 states render (loading skeleton / loaded rows / empty / error+retry / stale / offline) — never hidden.
  * i18n: widget.sentryEventLog + widget.noSentryEvents resolve from the P1/S10 catalog
    (apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json); derived titles/subtitles route through ILocalizer with the web
    English as the keyed fallback (the repo convention). No bare English literals.
  * accessibility: Narrator names on Refresh + error Retry and on every feed row; decorative icons set
    AccessibilityView=Raw; loading column is a polite live region.
  * diagnostics: view.opened slug=SentryEventLogWidget (PII-safe), asserted in tests.
  * registry: id sentry-event-log, category security, default 2x4, min 2x4, max 4x40 (asserted in tests).

